TruePix Repository — Multi-License Notice
=========================================

This repository aggregates several components under different open-source
licenses. There is no single license that covers every file. The authoritative
full license text for each component is the LICENSE file in that component's
directory (and, for Apache-2.0 components, any accompanying NOTICE).

Provenance of the TruePix core
------------------------------

The protocol implementation under `TruePix-main/` (and the video-editing front-end
under `VideoEdition/`) is the main contribution of this project. It is a
derivative work of the Hyrax interactive-proof codebase
(https://github.com/hyraxZK), substantially modified and extended for
verifiable video editing (TruePix).

Under Apache-2.0:

- Copyright in the original Hyrax material remains with the Hyrax authors
  (see notices below and in vendored Hyrax-derived components).
- Copyright in TruePix-specific modifications and new code belongs to the
  TruePix authors.

Retain both copyright lines when you redistribute those trees. A short
attribution also appears in `NOTICE`.

Component summary
-----------------

1. TruePix core (`TruePix-main/`, excluding vendored third-party trees under
   `TruePix-main/Orion/*/include/`) and `VideoEdition/`
   Apache License 2.0 — full text: `TruePix-main/LICENSE`
   Copyright (c) 2017 Riad S. Wahby and the Hyrax authors (original Hyrax code)
   Copyright (c) 2025–2026 the TruePix authors (modifications and new code)
   Replace "the TruePix authors" with your legal name or organization if desired.

2. libpws (`libpws/`)
   Apache License 2.0 — see `libpws/LICENSE`
   Copyright 2017 Riad S. Wahby and the Hyrax authors

3. pylaurent (`pylaurent/`)
   Apache License 2.0 — see `pylaurent/LICENSE`
   Copyright 2017 Riad S. Wahby and the Hyrax authors

4. pymiracl (`pymiracl/`)
   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0) — see `pymiracl/LICENSE`
   Copyright 2018 Riad S. Wahby and the Hyrax authors

   IMPORTANT: This repository includes and is designed to link against
   AGPL-3.0-licensed pymiracl. Redistributing a combined work that
   incorporates pymiracl, or providing a modified version as a network
   service, may trigger AGPL-3.0 obligations (including corresponding
   source disclosure). Review AGPL-3.0 carefully before redistributing
   or deploying.

5. Orion (`TruePix-main/Orion/Orion_zk/`, `TruePix-main/Orion/Orion_nonzk/`)
   Apache License 2.0 — see the LICENSE files in those directories
   Vendored dependencies under `include/` (for example XKCP and
